1
00:00:01,040 --> 00:00:01,260
Listen to this sound.

2
00:00:02,740 --> 00:00:04,100
Ch!

3
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,540
Two spellings make it.

4
00:00:09,540 --> 00:00:12,810
We can write ch, or we can write tch.

5
00:00:14,280 --> 00:00:17,780
You hear it in chair, and you hear it in catch.

6
00:00:19,520 --> 00:00:21,480
Same sound, different spelling.

7
00:00:22,120 --> 00:00:23,220
So which one do we write?

8
00:00:24,840 --> 00:00:26,920
We look at the letter just before it.

9
00:00:27,840 --> 00:00:28,820
Here is the rule.

10
00:00:29,740 --> 00:00:32,900
Right after a short vowel, we write tch.

11
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:34,720
Listen.

12
00:00:35,120 --> 00:00:37,340
C - a - tch.

13
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:39,260
Catch!

14
00:00:40,860 --> 00:00:43,720
That a is a short vowel, so we write tch.

15
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:46,360
Here are more.

16
00:00:47,760 --> 00:00:48,240
Match.

17
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:50,020
Watch.

18
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:52,260
Fetch.

19
00:00:53,800 --> 00:00:56,100
Everywhere else, we simply write ch.

20
00:00:57,040 --> 00:00:59,940
At the start of a word, nothing comes before it.

21
00:01:01,320 --> 00:01:01,540
Chair.

22
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:03,160
Chin.

23
00:01:04,560 --> 00:01:09,920
After a consonant, like the n in lunch.

24
00:01:11,700 --> 00:01:12,240
Bench.

25
00:01:13,520 --> 00:01:16,640
After a long vowel, which says its own name.

26
00:01:18,140 --> 00:01:18,240
Beach.

27
00:01:19,600 --> 00:01:19,900
Coach.

28
00:01:21,660 --> 00:01:23,200
All three take ch.

29
00:01:24,360 --> 00:01:25,160
But watch out!

30
00:01:25,520 --> 00:01:27,840
A few little words break this rule.

31
00:01:29,020 --> 00:01:34,780
Much, such, rich and which.

32
00:01:36,460 --> 00:01:39,080
They have short vowels, but they still use ch.

33
00:01:41,100 --> 00:01:42,440
Learn those four by heart.

34
00:01:42,760 --> 00:01:49,820
You will meet longer ones too, like ostrich and attach.

35
00:01:51,560 --> 00:01:52,390
Now, it is your turn!

36
00:01:53,400 --> 00:01:54,350
Here is the word.

37
00:01:55,360 --> 00:01:55,460
Beach.

38
00:01:56,700 --> 00:02:00,120
Is it ch, or tch?

39
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:02,910
It is ch!

40
00:02:03,740 --> 00:02:06,140
Because e and a make a long vowel.

41
00:02:07,100 --> 00:02:08,330
So let's remember it together.

42
00:02:09,700 --> 00:02:12,000
After a short vowel we write tch.

43
00:02:13,020 --> 00:02:15,680
Everywhere else we write just ch.

44
00:02:16,720 --> 00:02:19,600
And keep those few rule breakers in your pocket!

45
00:02:19,720 --> 00:02:22,760
Every spelling rule is waiting in the English Learning app.

46
00:02:23,640 --> 00:02:26,540
Download it today, and it will not cost you a thing!
